<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb silver imports down 36.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb silver imports down 36.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's silver imports in February fell by 36.6 percent from a year earlier to 84.69 tonnes, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The figures released by MOF were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Feb 97   Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> Total		84.69    130.00	133.53</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Mexico	     35.93     36.67	 18.00</p>
<p> U.S.		 43.02     70.63	 16.38</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first two months of 1997 totalled 214.69 tonnes against against 203.13 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk, +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
